---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import { Aside } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

import '../styles/data-tool.css';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Import Saved Data From Old vMenu',
    description: 'Turn everything the original vMenu saved on your computer into a vMenu Enhanced transfer code.',
    tableOfContents: false,
  }}
>
  <p>
    The original vMenu, v3.9.2 and older, saved your vehicles, peds, characters, weapon loadouts and
    settings in FiveM's storage folder on your computer. This page reads that folder, turns everything it
    finds into the vMenu Enhanced format, and gives you a transfer code to paste into the game. Everything
    happens in your browser. Nothing is uploaded anywhere.
  </p>

  <p>
    On FiveM Legacy, that storage folder is shared by every server you ever played on. So one import
    brings over everything you saved with the old vMenu, on any server.
  </p>

  <Aside type="danger" title="Close FiveM first">
    Close FiveM and its launcher completely before you open, copy or zip the folder, and keep them closed
    until this page shows you your code. FiveM keeps writing to this folder while it runs, and touching it at
    the same time can corrupt it, which wipes the saves of every server and script you use.
  </Aside>

  <Aside type="caution" title="At your own risk">
    The old vMenu and vMenu Enhanced store things very differently, so not everything converts perfectly.
    Clothes can come out as a different piece, some settings have no new version, and anything the page
    cannot read is skipped. The folder itself is never changed, so you can always try again.
  </Aside>

  <div class="vmt not-content">
    <div class="vmt-panel">
      <div class="vmt-label">Step 1. Copy the folder location</div>
      <p class="vmt-note">
        The old vMenu saved its data in this folder. Copy its location with the button, you will need it in
        the next step.
      </p>
      <div class="vmt-actions">
        <code id="vmi-path" class="vmt-path-box">%AppData%\CitizenFX\kvs</code>
        <button id="vmi-copy-path" class="vmt-button" type="button">Copy</button>
        <span id="vmi-path-status" class="vmt-status"></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="vmt-panel">
      <div class="vmt-label">Step 2. Pick the folder</div>
      <ol class="vmt-note vmt-steps">
        <li>Click <strong>Choose the kvs folder</strong>.</li>
        <li>Click the address bar at the top of the window that opens, paste the location with <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>V</kbd>, and press <kbd>Enter</kbd>.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Upload</strong> or <strong>Select Folder</strong>. Your browser may ask if you want to upload the files. Say yes, they still never leave your computer.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="vmt-actions">
        <button id="vmi-pick-folder" class="vmt-button vmt-primary" type="button">Choose the kvs folder</button>
        <button id="vmi-pick-zip" class="vmt-button" type="button">Choose a zip file instead</button>
        <input id="vmi-folder" class="vmt-file" type="file" webkitdirectory multiple />
        <input id="vmi-zip" class="vmt-file" type="file" accept=".zip,application/zip" />
      </div>
      <div id="vmi-drop" class="vmt-drop" tabindex="0">
        Or drag the <strong>kvs</strong> folder, the whole <strong>CitizenFX</strong> folder, or a zip of either one onto this box.
      </div>
      <div class="vmt-actions">
        <span id="vmi-status" class="vmt-status" role="status"></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="vmi-result" class="vmt-result" hidden>
      <div class="vmt-panel">
        <div id="vmi-summary"></div>
        <div id="vmi-resource-row" class="vmt-actions" hidden>
          <label class="vmt-row-label" for="vmi-resource">Found old vMenu data under more than one name. Use:</label>
          <select id="vmi-resource" class="vmt-input vmt-select"></select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="vmi-groups" class="vmt-groups"></div>

      <div class="vmt-panel vmt-sticky">
        <div id="vmi-warn" class="vmt-warn" hidden></div>
        <textarea id="vmi-code" class="vmt-code" spellcheck="false" readonly hidden></textarea>
        <div class="vmt-actions">
          <button id="vmi-copy" class="vmt-button vmt-primary" type="button">Copy my code</button>
          <button id="vmi-download" class="vmt-button" type="button">Download zip</button>
          <span id="vmi-out" class="vmt-status"></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Step 3. Paste it into the game</h2>

  <ol>
    <li>Start FiveM again and join a server running vMenu Enhanced.</li>
    <li>Open <strong>Misc Settings, Import &amp; Export</strong> and pick <strong>Paste A Code</strong>.</li>
    <li>Paste with <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>V</kbd> and press <kbd>Enter</kbd>.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    Paste A Code adds everything to what you already have. Anything saved under the same name in vMenu
    Enhanced is replaced by the imported one. More about codes is on{' '}
    <a href={`${base}/backing-up-your-data/`}>Backing Up Your Data</a>, and you can look through or change
    the code first with <a href={`${base}/data-editor/`}>Edit Your Data</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Already have saves in vMenu Enhanced?</h3>

  <p>
    Then you can pick what to keep before anything is replaced. In game, open <strong>Misc Settings,
    Import &amp; Export</strong> and pick <strong>Show My Transfer Code</strong> to get a code with your
    current saves. Paste that code and the one from this page into{' '}
    <a href={`${base}/data-compare/`}>Compare Or Merge Data</a>. It shows what is different, lets you choose
    which version of each item to keep, and gives you one merged code to paste into the game.
  </p>

  <h2>What comes over</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Old vMenu</th><th>In vMenu Enhanced</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Saved vehicles</td><td>Saved vehicles. They keep their old category, or go into <strong>Imported from old vMenu</strong> if they had none.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Saved peds</td><td>Saved peds, in the <strong>Imported from old vMenu</strong> category.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Saved multiplayer peds</td><td>Custom characters, with their face, hair, makeup, tattoos and outfit. They keep their old category, or go into <strong>Imported from old vMenu</strong> if they had none.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Weapon loadouts</td><td>Weapon loadouts, including which one loads when you respawn. Loadouts have no categories.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Your default character</td><td>Your default character.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Settings</td><td>Every setting that still exists. Settings that were removed or work differently now are left out.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>When something goes wrong</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>What you see</th><th>What to do</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>No old vMenu data was found</td><td>Make sure you picked <strong>kvs</strong>, not <strong>kvs_cl2</strong> or another folder. If you only ever played vMenu with GTA V Enhanced, there is nothing here to import.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Some files could not be read</td><td>FiveM was probably still running. Close FiveM and its launcher completely and pick the folder again.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>An item is listed as skipped</td><td>Its old save was damaged or used something vMenu Enhanced has no place for. Open it to see why.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>A character wears the wrong clothes</td><td>Fix the outfit in game and save it again. Clothes are stored differently now, so DLC pieces can shift.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</StarlightPage>

<script>
  import { setup } from '../scripts/legacy-import.js';

  setup();
</script>
